{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{artist: Matthew Bridges & George Elvey}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[D]Crown him with many [G]crowns, the [D]Lamb upon his [A]throne:
[D]hark how the heavenly [Em]anthem drowns all [A]music but its [D]own!
A[A]wake, my soul, and [D]sing of [G]him who [D]died for [A]thee,
and [D]hail him as thy [G]matchless King through [D]all e[A]terni[D]ty.

Verse 2
[D]Crown Him the virgin's [G]Son, the [D]God incarnate born, [A]Whose
[D]arm those crimson trophies [Em]won which [A]now His brow [D]adorn;
Fruit of the mystic [D]rose, as [G]of that [D]rose the [A]stem;
The [D]root whence mercy ever [G]flows, the Babe [D]of Bethlehem.

Verse 3
[D]Crown Him the Son [G]of God, before [D]the worlds began, [A]And
[D]ye who tread where He [Em]hath trod, crown [A]Him the Son of [D]Man;
Who every grief hath known [D]that wrings [G]the human [D]breast, And takes [A]and
bears [D]them for His own, that [G]all in Him [D]may rest.

Verse 4
[D]Crown Him the Lord [G]of life, who [D]triumphed o'er the [A]grave,
[D]And rose victorious in [Em]the strife for those [A]He came to [D]save.
His glories now we [D]sing, Who died, [G]and rose [D]on high, [A]Who
died [D]eternal life to bring, and [G]lives that death [D]may die.

Verse 5
[D]Crown Him the Lord [G]of peace, Whose [D]pow'r a scepter [A]sways
[D]From pole to pole, [Em]that wars may [A]cease, and all [D]be
prayer and praise. His [D]reign shall know [G]no end, [D]and round [A]His
pierced [D]feet Fair flow'rs of paradise [G]extend their fragrance [D]ever sweet.
